<h4 id="portfolio-grid-widget">Portfolio Grid</h4>
<p>
	The Portfolio Grid widget displays portfolio items in a grid or a single-row slider. In its settings, choose the layout, maximum number of items, sort order, and categories to display. You can also add a call-to-action item.
</p>

<h4 id="instagram-widget">Instagram Feed</h4>
<p>The theme uses <strong>Smash Balloon Social Photo Feed</strong> for Instagram feeds. The former ProteusThemes Instagram widget is no longer included.</p>
<ol>
	<li>Install and activate Smash Balloon Social Photo Feed from the theme's plugin installer.</li>
	<li>Open <strong>Instagram Feed &gt; All Feeds &gt; Add New</strong>, choose <strong>User Timeline</strong>, and add a source. Follow the plugin's account connection prompts.</li>
	<li>Customize and save the feed, then click <strong>Embed</strong> and copy its shortcode.</li>
	<li>Paste the shortcode into a SiteOrigin Editor widget on your page and save the page.</li>
</ol>
<p>For account requirements and connection help, follow <a href="https://smashballoon.com/doc/setting-up-the-free-instagram-feed-wordpress-plugin/" target="_blank">Smash Balloon's setup guide</a>. Configure the feed layout and refresh settings in the plugin.</p>

<h4 id="weather-widget">Weather Widget</h4>
<p>The Weather widget shows a location forecast. It uses a free OpenWeatherMap API key. You do not need a One Call subscription.</p>
<ol>
	<li>Follow <a href="https://openweathermap.org/guide#how_to_start" target="_blank">OpenWeatherMap's API key guide</a> to create an account and copy your key.</li>
	<li>Paste the key into the widget's <b>API key</b> field.</li>
	<li>Enter the location name, then the latitude and longitude. Look those up on <a href="https://www.latlong.net/" target="_blank">latlong.net</a>.</li>
	<li>Choose whether to show current weather in the main area, how many forecast days to display, and the temperature and wind units, then save the page.</li>
</ol>
<p>Weather data is cached for one hour. To refresh it sooner, edit the widget (for example, change the forecast length, update the page, then change it back).</p>
<p>If the widget still cannot retrieve forecasts after you add a key, update the theme to version 3.0.1 or later. Older versions called OpenWeather's discontinued One Call 2.5 API.</p>
